[{"id": 40730305, "text": "Apostrophes for Contraction", "modal": {"steps": [{"id": 40730167, "text": "<h2>What does an apostrophe look like?</h2>\nAn apostrophe looks like a comma but floating in the air between two letters. Here<span style=\"color:#E8492A\">'</span>s one!\n<br><br>\n<h2>What are apostrophes for?</h2>\nThere are several ways apostrophes can be used. In these activities, we are looking at apostrophes that show a letter or letters are missing. \n<br><br>\n<b>Examples of apostrophes where a letter or letters are missing:</b>\n<br>\nit<span style=\"color:#E8492A\">’</span>s → it <span style=\"color:#E8492A\">i</span>s           \n<br>don<span style=\"color:#E8492A\">’</span>t → do n<span style=\"color:#E8492A\">o</span>t            \n<br>she<span style=\"color:#E8492A\">’</span>s → she <span style=\"color:#E8492A\">i</span>s             \n<br>can<span style=\"color:#E8492A\">’</span>t → can<span style=\"color:#E8492A\">no</span>t\n<br><br>\n<b>And one slightly odd one…</b>\n<br>\nwon<span style=\"color:#E8492A\">’</span>t → will n<span style=\"color:#E8492A\">o</span>t\n<br>The English language and spelling has changed over time, and “won’t” is actually short for “woll not”. We say “will not” now, but the old spelling has stuck in the short version “won’t”.\n<br></br>\n<h2>Why is this called 'contraction'?</h2>\nBecause 'contraction' means 'becoming smaller' - the words become smaller when the letters are missed out and an apostrophe is used instead.", "order": 1, "btnType": null, "linkUrl": null, "modalId": 29, "audioUrl": null, "fileName": null, "fontSize": null, "fontType": "SassoonInfantRg-Regular", "imageUrl": null, "linkName": null, "stepType": "TEXT_AND_IMAGE", "tabsData": null, "deletedAt": null, "tableData": "{\"headers\":[\"Col1\"],\"rows\":[{\"col1\":\"row1\"},{\"col1\":\"row2\"}, {\"col1\":\"row3\"}]}", "timerData": null, "activityId": null, "dimensions": null, "editAsHtml": false, "properties": {"height": "", "fontArray": [[]], "inputArray": [[]], "widthArray": [[""]]}, "deletedById": null, "downloadUrl": null, "editorState": null, "carouselData": null, "downloadName": null, "accordionData": null, "includeSeconds": null, "selectedModalId": 0, "textCarouselData": "{ \"text\": [] }", "checkListTextData": null, "imageCarouselData": null, "checklistImageData": null, "clickableAlphabetData": null}], "details": {"id": 29, "name": "Apostrophes for Contraction", "logCreatedAt": "2021-11-08T15:28:58.973847", "logUpdatedAt": "2021-11-08T15:34:56.348823", "logCreatedById": null, "logUpdatedById": null, "nameForContentDev": null}}, "order": 4, "btnType": "SECONDARY", "linkUrl": null, "audioUrl": null, "fileName": null, "fontSize": null, "fontType": "SassoonInfantRg-Regular", "imageUrl": null, "linkName": null, "stepType": "MODAL", "tabsData": null, "deletedAt": null, "tableData": "{\"headers\":[\"Col1\"],\"rows\":[{\"col1\":\"row1\"},{\"col1\":\"row2\"}, {\"col1\":\"row3\"}]}", "timerData": null, "activityId": 36575834, "dimensions": null, "editAsHtml": false, "properties": {"height": "", "fontArray": [[]], "inputArray": [[]], "widthArray": [[""]]}, "deletedById": null, "downloadUrl": null, "editorState": null, "carouselData": null, "downloadName": null, "accordionData": null, "includeSeconds": null, "selectedModalId": 29, "textCarouselData": "{ \"text\": [] }", "checkListTextData": null, "imageCarouselData": null, "checklistImageData": null, "clickableAlphabetData": null}, {"id": 40729987, "text": "<h2>The Activity:</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Spread the cards face down on the table.</li>\n<li>Player 1 turns over one card and reads what is on it, e.g. “it’s”</li>\n<li>Player 1 then says what other card they are hoping for, e.g. “it is” if they already turned over “it’s”.</li>\n<li>Player 1 turns over a second card. If it goes with their first card, they keep both and have another turn. If it doesn’t match, they turn both cards back over and it is Player 2’s turn.</li>\n<li>Take it in turns to turn over cards until all the cards are gone. The person with the most cards at the end is the winner!</li>\n</ol>", "modal": {"steps": [null], "details": null}, "order": 5, "btnType": null, "linkUrl": null, "audioUrl": null, "fileName": null, "fontSize": null, "fontType": "SassoonInfantRg-Regular", "imageUrl": null, "linkName": null, "stepType": "TEXT_AND_IMAGE", "tabsData": null, "deletedAt": null, "tableData": "{\"headers\":[\"Col1\"],\"rows\":[{\"col1\":\"row1\"},{\"col1\":\"row2\"}, {\"col1\":\"row3\"}]}", "timerData": null, "activityId": 36575834, "dimensions": null, "editAsHtml": false, "properties": {"height": "", "fontArray": [[]], "inputArray": [[]], "widthArray": [[""]]}, "deletedById": null, "downloadUrl": null, "editorState": null, "carouselData": null, "downloadName": null, "accordionData": null, "includeSeconds": null, "selectedModalId": 0, "textCarouselData": "{ \"text\": [] }", "checkListTextData": null, "imageCarouselData": null, "checklistImageData": null, "clickableAlphabetData": null}, {"id": 36576891, "text": "<h2>Short of Space?</h2>\nYou could try using the same cards to play snap. Pile the cards face down and take it in turns to turn over a card. Each time you turn one over, read what is on it and say what it’s pair would be (like in the Memory Card game).", "modal": {"steps": [null], "details": null}, "order": 6, "btnType": null, "linkUrl": null, "audioUrl": null, "fileName": null, "fontSize": null, "fontType": null, "imageUrl": null, "linkName": null, "stepType": "TEXT_AND_IMAGE", "tabsData": null, "deletedAt": null, "tableData": null, "timerData": null, "activityId": 36575834, "dimensions": null, "editAsHtml": false, "properties": {"inputArray": [[]]}, "deletedById": null, "downloadUrl": null, "editorState": null, "carouselData": null, "downloadName": null, "accordionData": null, "includeSeconds": null, "selectedModalId": null, "textCarouselData": null, "checkListTextData": null, "imageCarouselData": null, "checklistImageData": null, "clickableAlphabetData": null}, {"